From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 03:02:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Key the block-position collections by packed long

The four collections keyed by BlockPosition now use fastutil primitive
containers keyed by BlockPosition.asLong():

  Chunk.tileEntities            -> Long2ObjectOpenHashMap
  World.capturedTileEntities    -> Long2ObjectOpenHashMap
  BlockRedstoneWire.blocksNeedingUpdate -> LongOpenHashSet
  AntiXray.pendingUpdates       -> LongOpenHashSet

BlockPosition already carried a lossless 26/12/26-bit layout in
asLong()/fromLong(), so the packing is its own, not a new scheme; pack()
and unpackX/Y/Z() are added so callers can populate and read these
collections by coordinate without building a position to hash.

Beyond dropping the position objects the maps used to retain, this
removes allocations at the call sites: BlockRedstoneWire built six
positions via shift() on every wire update, and AntiXray's
updateNearbyBlocks recursed through six neighbour positions per level at
radius 2. Both now work in ints.

CraftChunk.getTileEntities() needed fixing in the same change: it looped
over keySet() with an `instanceof BlockPosition` guard, which after this
would have matched nothing and quietly returned an array of nulls
instead of failing. It now unpacks the long keys.

Chunk.getTileEntities() returns Long2ObjectMap<TileEntity> - a
deliberate NMS signature change; every in-tree caller only uses values().

BlockPositionPackTest checks pack/unpack round trips across the full
coordinate range, agreement with asLong()/fromLong(), and that
neighbouring positions cannot collide.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockPosition.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockPosition.java
index 1ef22fc8ec8dedf8adfc28dc4b11897eb05e5673..6f7cd47a61f608c8e441efae47408ce37d461b57 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockPosition.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/BlockPosition.java
@@ -153,6 +153,25 @@ public class BlockPosition extends BaseBlockPosition {
         return ((long) this.getX() & BlockPosition.X_MASK) << BlockPosition.X_SHIFT | ((long) this.getY() & BlockPosition.Y_MASK) << BlockPosition.Y_SHIFT | ((long) this.getZ() & BlockPosition.Z_MASK) << 0;
     }
 
+    // Athena start - pack/unpack without building a BlockPosition, so long-keyed collections can be
+    // populated and read by coordinate. Same layout as asLong()/fromLong().
+    public static long pack(int x, int y, int z) {
+        return ((long) x & BlockPosition.X_MASK) << BlockPosition.X_SHIFT | ((long) y & BlockPosition.Y_MASK) << BlockPosition.Y_SHIFT | ((long) z & BlockPosition.Z_MASK) << 0;
+    }
+
+    public static int unpackX(long i) {
+        return (int) (i << 64 - BlockPosition.X_SHIFT - BlockPosition.NUM_X_BITS >> 64 - BlockPosition.NUM_X_BITS);
+    }
+
+    public static int unpackY(long i) {
+        return (int) (i << 64 - BlockPosition.Y_SHIFT - BlockPosition.NUM_Y_BITS >> 64 - BlockPosition.NUM_Y_BITS);
+    }
+
+    public static int unpackZ(long i) {
+        return (int) (i << 64 - BlockPosition.NUM_Z_BITS >> 64 - BlockPosition.NUM_Z_BITS);
+    }
+    // Athena end
+
     public static BlockPosition fromLong(long i) {
         int j = (int) (i << 64 - BlockPosition.X_SHIFT - BlockPosition.NUM_X_BITS >> 64 - BlockPosition.NUM_X_BITS);
         int k = (int) (i << 64 - BlockPosition.Y_SHIFT - BlockPosition.NUM_Y_BITS >> 64 - BlockPosition.NUM_Y_BITS);
